id: DRAFT-12412-zsa-wally-cgo-pkgconfig-prefix-rewrite
category: build-system, conan, cgo, go, libusb, pkg-config
build_system: custom|go
phase: build
match_keywords: cgo pkg-config, gousb, libusb-1.0, prefix=/usr/local, PKG_CONFIG_PATH, PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR, CGO_CFLAGS, CGO_LDFLAGS, pc file, autotools DESTDIR, conan package_info, pkgconfig dir, #cgo directive
error_signature: "cgo: 'pkg-config --cflags --libs libusb-1.0' resolves include/lib paths against /usr/local (system prefix baked into the registry package's lib/pkgconfig/libusb-1.0.pc) instead of the Conan dependency package folder; build picks up host headers or fails with 'libusb.h: No such file or directory'"
error_excerpt: "pkg-config --cflags libusb-1.0 -> -I/usr/local/include/libusb-1.0 (wrong: registry artifact lives in ~/.conan2/p/...; the .pc was installed by autotools with DESTDIR=<pkg> prefix= leaving prefix=/usr/local)"
root_cause: "The ohpcd registry libusb/1.0.27 recipe installs via autotools 'make install DESTDIR=<package_folder> prefix='; libtool's pkgconfig file records prefix=/usr/local (the empty --prefix with DESTDIR does not rewrite libdir/includedir in the generated .pc). Any CGO build (#cgo pkg-config: libusb-1.0) that trusts pkg-config therefore gets -I/usr/local/include/libusb-1.0 and -L/usr/local/lib — host paths that do not exist on the OHOS device/CI worker. The conan package_info does ship cpp_info.includedirs/libdirs correctly, but the #cgo directive in the Go dependency (gousb) goes through pkg-config, not through conan generators."
rec_approach: "rewrite the .pc prefix next to the build + inject CGO flags explicitly"
solution: "In generate()/build(), copy the dependency's lib/pkgconfig/libusb-1.0.pc into <build_folder>/pkgconfig/ replacing 'prefix=/usr/local' with 'prefix=<dependency package_folder>'; export PKG_CONFIG_PATH and PKG_CONFIG_LIBDIR to that dir. Belt-and-braces: also set CGO_CFLAGS=-I<pkg>/include/libusb-1.0 and CGO_LDFLAGS=-L<pkg>/lib -lusb-1.0 so the cgo toolchain resolves flags even when pkg-config is missing/misbehaving on the worker. Synthesize a minimal .pc from the package layout when the source .pc is absent. See archives/z/zsa-wally/2.0.1/conanfile.py _libusb_paths() (used by both generate() and the go-test audit env)."
fallback: "If the registry recipe is ever fixed to install a conan-correct .pc (prefix rewritten at package time), the rewrite step becomes a no-op and only the CGO_CFLAGS/CGO_LDFLAGS explicit injection is needed; alternatively a pure-C consumer can use conan generators (CMakeDeps/pkg_config generator) which already emit correct paths."
prescan_pattern: "#cgo pkg-config|libusb-1.0.pc|prefix=/usr/local"
verify_builds: "PR #14957 (task #12412) local conan create ohos-aarch64: rc=0 with CGO_ENABLED=1 building gousb v2.1.0 against registry libusb/1.0.27; test_package runs the linked binary (libusb-1.0.so.0 NEEDED, VirtualRunEnv provides LD_LIBRARY_PATH) 6/6 assertions"
severity: 2
last_updated: 2026-10-08
